<article class="env-definition" id="06CF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06CF">Definition <span data-tag="06CF">97.8.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $F : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ be a $1$-morphism of stacks in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. We say that $F$ is <em>algebraic</em> if for every scheme $T$ and every object $\xi $ of $\mathcal{Y}$ over $T$ the $2$-fibre product </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  (\mathit{Sch}/T)_{fppf} \times _{\xi , \mathcal{Y}} \mathcal{X}  \]
</div>
  <p> is an algebraic stack over $S$. </p>
</article>